{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"12/11/2026 13:20:16","profile":{"player_id":"64859","last_updated":"12/11/2026 13:20","fullname":"Gamachchi Withanage Hasini Madushika Perera","short_display_name":"H Perera","name":"Hasini Perera","gender":"F","dob":"27/06/1995","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"Sri Lanka","nationality_id":"8","nationality":"Sri Lanka","nationality_short_code":"SL","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"1","text":"Batsman","role":"Batter"},"batting_style":{"id":"2","text":"Left Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"12","text":"Right-arm medium fast"},"writeup":"<p>Hasini Perera is a skilled Sri Lankan cricketer born on June 27, 1995. She made her international debut in 2014, marking her T20I debut against Bangladesh in April and her ODI debut against South Africa in October of the same year. Since then, she has become an integral part of Sri Lanka's women's cricket team.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nPerera has represented Sri Lanka in several major international tournaments. She was part of the squad for the 2018 ICC Women's World Twenty20 in the West Indies and the 2020 ICC Women's T20 World Cup in Australia. Her consistent performances and contributions to the team have earned her a spot in various high-profile events.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nPerera's recent appearances include the 2021 Women's Cricket World Cup Qualifier in Zimbabwe, the 2022 Commonwealth Games Cricket Qualifier in Malaysia, and the 2022 Commonwealth Games in Birmingham, England. She was also named in Sri Lanka's squad for the 2024 ICC Women's T20 World Cup and once again in the upcoming 2025 ODI World Cup, further highlighting her importance to the team.&nbsp;</p>","relation":null,"social_details":{"social_platform":[{"social_platform_id":"1","social_platform_name":"facebook","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"2","social_platform_name":"twitter","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"3","social_platform_name":"instagram","social_platform_url":"https://www.instagram.com/hasiniperera7/"},{"social_platform_id":"4","social_platform_name":"youtube","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"5","social_platform_name":"pinterest","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"6","social_platform_name":"linkedin","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"7","social_platform_name":"josh","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"8","social_platform_name":"moj","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"9","social_platform_name":"chingari","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"10","social_platform_name":"mx_takatak","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"11","social_platform_name":"tiktok","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"12","social_platform_name":"koo","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"13","social_platform_name":"clubhouse","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"14","social_platform_name":"telegram","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"15","social_platform_name":"sharechat","social_platform_url":""},{"social_platform_id":"16","social_platform_name":"snapchat","social_platform_url":""}]},"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"1133","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"Sri Lanka"},{"id":"1987","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Sri lanka Emerging"},{"id":"5250","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Palink Sports Club"},{"id":"5254","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Combined Provinces"},{"id":"5255","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Western Province"},{"id":"5259","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Colombo District"},{"id":"5266","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Sri Lanka Navy Sports Club"},{"id":"5268","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"SLC Greens"}]},"international_debut":{"comp_type_id":"13","comp_